## 2. Nerf the units: it takes more Launch Point to be launched hard

### Current behaviour
`js/data/launch.js`: `LAUNCH_UNIT_SPEED = 10`. It's the one conversion from launch strength (Base Launch × Launch Point) to world speed, used by `resolveDirectionalLaunch` (`speed = strength * LAUNCH_UNIT_SPEED`). The game's numbers stay as they are; only the physics' speed per point changes.

### Wanted
Change `LAUNCH_UNIT_SPEED` from **10 to 7**. This value is decided, so use exactly 7 and don't tune it to anything else. The same Launch Point and Base Launch then send a fighter less far: 30 Launch Point × Base Launch 2 = strength 60 used to be 600 units/s and is now 420. A fighter needs about 43 % more Launch Point (≈ 43 instead of 30) to be launched as hard as before. Keep it as the single tuning knob, so the owner can later try 8 or 6 by editing that one line. Add a comment explaining why it went from 10 to 7 (the **launch & energy update**: launches nerfed without touching Base Launch, Launch Point or damage). Don't change Base Launch, Launch Point or damage (see **Off limits**).

Check everything that depends on launch speed rather than strength, and say in `UPDATES.md` whether you deliberately left each one alone or re-tuned it:
- `js/game/combat/launch-bounce.js` (`LAUNCH_BOUNCE`; a comment there assumes "At LAUNCH_UNIT_SPEED 10…"). Rewrite that comment for 7. Only keep the bounce thresholds feeling the same if they were tuned around 10.
- `launchReaction` (`stunPerThousand`, `tumbleSpeed`, in `combat.js` and each character's data): these are in units/s, so hitstun and tumble will kick in later. That's expected and part of the nerf. Don't raise them back.
- CPU: `js/game/ai/cpu-intelligence/values.js` (`st.baseLaunch * lp * LAUNCH_UNIT_SPEED`) reads the constant, so it follows automatically. Check `prediction.js`, `evaluator.js`, `objective.js` and `plans.js` for any hard-coded kill / "launch hard" Launch Point thresholds or speeds that assumed 10, and switch them to derive from the constant.
- The reference copy (`LAUNCH_FORMULA` etc. in `launch.js` and localization) if it names the number.
- Tests that assert exact launch speeds (`tests/systems/launch.test.mjs`, `launch-bounce.test.mjs`, `launch-reaction.test.mjs`, `combat-rules.test.mjs`, fighter tests): update them to compute from `LAUNCH_UNIT_SPEED` instead of literals. Add a test that a fixed Launch Point / Base Launch now produces `strength × 7` and that strength itself is unchanged.

