## 3. A perfect Shield takes 5 off the Launch Point

### Current behaviour
In `CombatSystem.applyHit` (`js/game/combat/combat.js` ~line 517), `perfect = blocked && !!target.perfectShield` (see `Fighter.perfectShield`: raised within `defense.perfectWindow` after `perfectRearm`). It blocks with no blockstun and pays the normal `shieldHitCost`. It doesn't affect the Launch Point.

### Wanted
Every perfect block also takes **5** Launch Points off the **blocking** fighter, never below 0. Use `CombatState.heal(5)` so it counts in `launchPointRecovered` and, like any heal, doesn't restart or speed up the passive recovery schedule. Add the amount as a named constant, e.g. `PERFECT_SHIELD_HEAL = 5`, in `js/data/launch.js` or with the defense data, the same for every fighter. Record it on the block event (e.g. `heal: 5`, or the actual amount taken off, plus the real `launchPointAfter`) so the HUD, the match stats and the effects can see it. Only a perfect block does this. One perfect block heals once, even for a multi-hit string, since a blocked string stops at the first block anyway; check that. It's simulation state, so online lockstep must stay deterministic (`tests/online/determinism.test.mjs`, `lockstep.test.mjs`).

Tests (`tests/systems/defense.test.mjs` / `shield-protection.test.mjs`): a perfect block at LP 12 leaves 7, at LP 3 leaves 0, a normal block leaves LP unchanged, and the recovery timer is untouched.

