## 7. Deflect only costs Energy when it turns a projectile back

### Current behaviour
`Fighter.tryDeflect` (`fighter.js` ~line 1507) pays `energyDef.deflectCost` (`DEFLECT_ENERGY_COST = 15`, `js/data/energy.js`) **as it starts**, whatever it then meets. Projectiles are turned back in `CombatSystem.deflectProjectiles` (`combat.js` ~line 345), which pushes `{ fighter, projectile, from, direction }` into `this.deflections`. The docs in `js/game/combat/deflect.js`, `energy.js`, `combat-state.js` and `fighter.js` all say "paid as it starts".

### Wanted
- Starting a Deflect costs nothing. It still needs the fighter **not exhausted** (`canUseEnergy()`), as now, so an exhausted fighter still can't Deflect.
- The cost is paid **once per Deflect activation, the first time it actually turns a projectile back**. Turning back several projectiles in the same Deflect, on one step or across its active phase, still costs 15 once. Store a `paid` flag on that attack instance (`combat.attack`). A Deflect that only strikes a fighter (its melee hit, blocked or not), or whiffs, or is cancelled before turning anything back, costs **nothing**.
- Pay it through the same path as other spending (`payEnergy` / `spendEnergy`, setting `energyPaidAt` so there's no refill that step, and with less than 15 left it empties the bar and exhausts). If the fighter is somehow exhausted at the moment of the deflection, the projectile is still turned back; the Deflect already started legally. Don't make the deflection depend on whether it could pay.
- Record the cost on the deflection entry (`energyCost`) for effects, stats and the CPU.
- Update every comment and doc that says "paid as it starts", `ENERGY_COST`'s summary and the in-game Deflect description.
- Tests (`tests/systems/deflect.test.mjs`, `energy.test.mjs`): a whiffed Deflect costs 0. One that hits a fighter but turns nothing back costs 0. One that turns back one projectile costs 15. One that turns back two costs 15. An exhausted fighter still can't start one. No refill on the step it pays.

## 8. Shield only costs Energy when it actually blocks something

The Shield should already pay only on a block (`applyHit`: `if (blocked) spendEnergy(shieldHitCost)`), and refill keeps running while it's held. **Audit this and make sure it holds**, then lock it in with tests:
- Raising, holding or lowering the Shield, and perfect-Shield timing, cost nothing.
- `blocked = tc.shielding` is decided before anything else in `applyHit`. Check every caller and every early-return path so Energy is only taken when a hit really **reached** the fighter and was stopped: hits that `hitReaches` passes by (`quake` on an airborne fighter, `gaze` on one facing away), a charmed attacker's "hit" (`charmed()`), stage and platform hazards (`stage-hazards.js`, `platform-hazards.js`), projectiles that `passed()` the target, piercing/erasing projectiles, summon/clone strikes and technique bursts. Each one pays only if it is actually blocked, and only once per blocked hit. If any path takes Energy from the Shield for something it didn't block, or takes it twice for one hit, fix it.
- Keep the existing rules: a block costs `shieldHitCost` (perfect included, as now), or whatever is left if that's less, and a block that empties the bar drops the Shield.
- Tests (`tests/systems/shield-protection.test.mjs`, `energy.test.mjs`): holding the Shield for N seconds with nothing hitting it loses no Energy (it refills). One blocked hit costs exactly 15. A quake that passes over / a gaze from behind / a passed projectile cost nothing.

